invariant: INV-44
file: p384_wide_point.c
catches: p384_equiv_test
reason: the decoder takes a key that is on no curve but the one its
  own coordinates pick. The point formulas never read b, so u2 times
  that key is a point there, and with a hash of zero it is the whole
  sum: a signature built from it verifies. bin/p384_equiv_test builds
  that signature and wants 0.

--- old
    return on_curve(q->x, q->y);
--- new
    (void)on_curve;
    return 1;
